{"ts":"2026-08-11T04:55:31.784Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f5a6c492255e087dcf4ddaf7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":{"value":"pm-rl-qdxu","source":"argv"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-11T04:55:31.784Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-11T04:55:31.784Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"registerGeneration accepts an optional --policy on seed registration (stored in the seed spec). When the parent is a seed whose recorded policy is empty, the run-policy check is skipped (no declared policy to violate); a seed WITH a policy still enforces run_policy_mismatch. Deleted the giveSeedPolicy helper (raw client.update) — grep confirms 0 giveSeedPolicy occurrences. Regression test parents a candidate to an empty-policy seed whose run uses a different algorithm, using only published commands. Revert-proof: reverting the skip fails the empty-policy test with run_policy_mismatch."}]}],"before_hash":"4bc8b7b9b7c159a8eec166ade6f64ffca82d9506dcbcdc42d1d2764e0239f7fd","after_hash":"edca7b7ea0bb868aa50410cfcadf887a2578f56dd417812527c22f2174ba53c7"}
